  "body": "Consider a pattern intended to match dotfiles like `new URLPattern({ pathname: '/.*' })`.  The pathname encoding algorithm will end up collapsing the `/.` to just `.` so you get a final pattern of `/*`.\r\n\r\nTo work around this issue you can isolate the dot in a custom regexp group like `/(\\\\.)*`.\r\n\r\nThis is forked off from #156.",
